      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks prof. i guess i'm just sensitive to it. but that \"skittering\" part is really what sticks with me. it's like there's this constant, tiny, irritating scratching happening right at the front of my mouth. when it's /s/ or /ʃ/ it feels almost like a swarm of tiny, frantic things making a mess of the airway. is there any linguistic reason why certain sounds feel so much more \"chaotic\" or \"nuisance-like\" than others?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
