      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The feeling of \"chaotic\" or \"nuisance-like\" sounds is fascinating, and it often relates to the *acoustic* properties of the sounds, not just the physical articulation. Sounds that create high levels of turbulent noise, like /s/ and /ʃ/, have a very high spectral energy distribution, which our brains often perceive as sharp, harsh, or even irritating. This high-frequency, noisy quality is what makes them feel \"frantic,\" much like the sound of a swarm of tiny, agitated things. It's a sensory experience layered onto the phonetic reality.",
